💡 **SUGGESTION: [readOutcomeMeta] matches the truncation notice anywhere in the result**

`RegExp(r'\[Showing lines (\d+)-(\d+) of (\d+)\.').firstMatch(trimmed)` scans the WHOLE result text, not just its tail. The read tool appends the notice at the end, but a read whose CONTENT quotes the pattern — session JSONLs, harness logs, docs about this very harness — misreports the row as `N of M lines read` (agents read session files regularly in this repo, and those embed past notices).

Two cheap tightenings:

```dart
// anchor to the tail: the notice is always the last line of a truncated read
final notice = trimmed.split('\n').last;
final match = RegExp(r'^\[Showing lines (\d+)-(\d+) of (\d+)\.').firstMatch(notice);
```

or drop the special case entirely and always count the shown text's lines. Cosmetic either way (a dim meta fragment), so no rush.

💡 **SUGGESTION: doc overstates what [transcriptExpandDetails] toggles**

The doc says "collapsed thinking rows **and previews** by default; `all` renders the persisted detail under each collapsed row" — but the flag only gates the THINKING detail. The bash command preview (`previewLines` in `tuiToolCard`) renders unconditionally in both states, and nothing re-renders already-emitted rows (rows after the switch only). Also worth stating: the state is process-scoped — a restarted `fa` replays collapsed again (`/transcript` is not a persisted setting, per the cli_parity entry).

Suggested wording:

```dart
/// The expanded/collapsed transcript state (`/transcript expand all|none`,
/// gh-193 interaction): thinking rows render collapsed (`> Thought for Ns`)
/// by default; `all` renders their persisted text under the label. Affects
/// rows emitted after the switch and the in-process `/resume` replay; bash
/// previews always render. Process-scoped: a restart replays collapsed.
```

💡 **SUGGESTION: `/transcript` silently does nothing outside the TUI chrome face**

`_handleTranscriptCommand` is dispatched in both the TUI REPL and the line-mode/headless REPL, and it confirms `transcript: expanded` — but on the non-TUI faces nothing observable changes: line mode never collapses thinking (it streams dim per-delta or not at all, `_streamsThinking`), line-mode replay renders thinking NEVER (the AC5 REG pins it), and the closed thinking window only opens under `_useTui && tuiChromeEnabled`.

Consider having the reply say so, e.g.:

```dart
if (!_useTui || !tuiChromeEnabled) {
  io.writeln('transcript expand only affects the TUI chrome transcript');
  return;
}
```

(or gate the command case on `_useTui` and fall through to the usage line). Purely informational — the state flag itself is harmless elsewhere.

💡 **SUGGESTION: doc placement — the diffstat is composed/painted BEFORE the meta, not after**

`ToolCardSegments.diffstat`'s doc says "squeezed in **after** the meta", but both the composition (`'$descRaw$badgeRaw$diffRaw$metaRaw'` in `_squeezeCardTail`) and the paint order (`desc, badge, diff, meta` in `_paintCardTail`) place it BEFORE the meta; the squeeze order (meta drops first, then the diffstat) is documented correctly on `_squeezeCardTail` itself. One word fix so the next reader doesn't chase the wrong visual order:

```dart
/// ... painted in the `toolDiffAdded`/`toolDiffRemoved` roles, squeezed in
/// before the meta (meta drops first when the row is tight).
```

# Garbled doc on `DiffStat.label` — reworded

Fixed on this head (`lib/src/cli/tool_row_content.dart`, `DiffStat.label`):

```dart
/// The RAW `+N −M` label: an ASCII `+`, then U+212 MINUS SIGN before
/// the removal count, between regular spaces — matching the ticket
/// grammar (and [paintDiffstat]'s `^\+(\d+) −(\d+)$`) verbatim.
String get label => isEmpty ? '' : '+$added −$removed';
```

The ™/“thin-space free” wording is gone; the doc now names the actual characters (ASCII `+`, U+212 MINUS SIGN, plain spaces) and points at the `paintDiffstat` regex that consumes the label.

# `transcriptExpandDetails` doc overstated its scope — corrected

Fixed on this head (`lib/src/cli/tool_row_content.dart`), adopting the suggested wording:

```dart
/// The expanded/collapsed transcript state (`/transcript expand all|none`,
/// gh-1933 interaction): thinking rows render collapsed (`> Thought for
/// Ns`) by default; `all` renders their persisted text under the label.
/// Affects rows emitted after the switch and the in-process `/resume`
/// replay; bash previews always render. Process-scoped: a restart replays
/// collapsed (review thread PRRT_kwDOTXdlLc6w5WCs — `/transcript` is not a
/// persisted setting).
```

The “and previews” claim is gone, the rows-after-the-switch semantics and the process-scoped lifetime are stated. The matching `test/skills/cli_parity_test.dart` entry now says process-scoped + TUI-chrome-only as well.

# `/transcript` silently did nothing outside the TUI chrome face — it now says so

Fixed on this head (`lib/src/cli/agent_cli_commands.dart`, `_handleTranscriptCommand`), per the suggested guard:

```dart
case 'expand all' || 'expand none' || 'collapse':
  if (!_useTui || !tuiChromeEnabled) {
    io.writeln('transcript expand only affects the TUI chrome transcript');
    return;
  }
```

The mutating arms answer the informational line on line-mode/headless faces and **leave the render state alone** (no hidden `transcriptExpandDetails` flip that could never render there). Bare `/transcript` still reports the state + usage anywhere.

Pinned by the updated `/transcript expand toggles the collapsed-detail state` test in `test/cli/agent_cli_test.dart`, which runs on the line-mode face and now asserts the informational reply and that the flag stays `false`.

# `ToolCardSegments.diffstat` doc placement — corrected to “before the meta”

Fixed on this head (`lib/src/cli/tui_chrome.dart:107`):

```dart
/// The applied-change diffstat (`+N −M`, gh-1933 AC2) — painted in the
/// `toolDiffAdded`/`toolDiffRemoved` roles, squeezed in BEFORE the meta
/// (review thread PRRT_kwDOTXdlLc6w5WJc: meta drops first when the row
/// is tight — see [_squeezeCardTail]).
```

Now matches both the composition order (`desc, badge, diff, meta` in `_squeezeCardTail`) and the paint order in `_paintCardTail`; the squeeze precedence (meta drops first, then the diffstat) is cross-referenced.
